"summary": "Implemented chat allow/deny list enforcement server-side. In src/messaging/index.js (canMessageUser), the old restrictChat/isFollowing check was replaced: admins and global moderators bypass all chat restrictions; otherwise, attempts are blocked with exactly [[error:chat-restricted]] when (1) the recipient disabled incoming chats, (2) the sender is on the recipient's deny list (deny list checked first, taking precedence), or (3) the recipient's allow list is non-empty and the sender is not on it. Blocked users still get [[error:chat-user-blocked]]; with both lists empty and incoming chats enabled, anyone not blocked can chat. In src/user/settings.js, getSettings now exposes disableIncomingChats (boolean) and chatAllowList/chatDenyList (parsed uid arrays via a new parseChatList helper that tolerates raw/JSON/array values), and saveSettings persists the three new fields so users can manage them through the settings API. Limitation: apply_edits requires a non-empty old_text, so creating the new migration file src/upgrades/1.19.0/chat_allow_deny_lists.js was rejected by the tool; the upgrade (seeding uid:{uid}:chat:allow from follows for accounts with restrictChat enabled, idempotently skipping non-empty lists) could not be added and remains unimplemented. Enforcement is server-side; UI templates for the user-facing toggles were not modified.",
